age will include a detailed data report in both TSV and JSONL formats.\n\nFile name \n\n  Download\n\n## [Summary](#)\n\n[Go to the top of the page](#top \"Go to the top of the page\") [Help](/books/NBK3841/#EntrezGene.Summary_2 \"Help\")\n\nOfficial Symbol\n\nPADI6provided by [HGNC](http://www.genenames.org/ \"HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee\")\n\nOfficial Full Name\n\npeptidyl arginine deiminase 6provided by [HGNC](http://www.genenames.org/ \"HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee\")\n\nPrimary source\n\n[HGNC:HGNC:20449](https://www.genenames.org/data/gene-symbol-report/#!/hgnc_id/HGNC:20449)\n\nSee related\n\n[Ensembl:ENSG00000276747](http://www.ensembl.org/id/ENSG00000276747) [MIM:610363;](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/omim/610363) [AllianceGenome:HGNC:20449](https://www.alliancegenome.org/gene/HGNC:20449)\n\nGene type\n\nprotein coding\n\nRefSeq status\n\nREVIEWED\n\nOrganism\n\n[Homo sapiens](/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?id=9606)\n\nLineage\n\nEukaryota; Metazoa; Chordata; Craniata; Vertebrata; Euteleostomi; Mammalia; Eutheria; Euarchontoglires; Primates; Haplorrhini; Catarrhini; Hominidae; Homo\n\nAlso known as\n\nhPADVI; OZEMA16; PREMBL2\n\nSummary\n\nThis gene encodes a member of the peptidyl arginine deiminase family of enzymes, which catalyze the post-translational deimination of proteins by converting arginine residues into citrullines in the presence of calcium ions. The family members have distinct substrate specificities and tissue-specific expression patterns. This protein may play a role in cytoskeletal reorganization in the egg and in early embryo development. \\[provided by RefSeq, Sep 2012\\]\n\nExpression\n\nLow expression observed in reference dataset [See more](#gene-expression)\n\nOrthologs\n\n[all](/datasets/gene/353238/#orthologs)\n\n**Try the new [Gene page](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/datasets/gene/353238/)**  \n**Try the new [Transcripts and proteins table](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/datasets/gene/353238/#transcripts-and-proteins)**\n\n## 