t in a consanguineous Chinese family caused by a novel missense variant of PADI6.](/pubmed/37220902/) Zhang M, *et al*. QJM, 2023 Oct 6. PMID 37220902\n5.  [Myocardial citrullination in rheumatoid arthritis: a correlative histopathologic study.](/pubmed/22364592/) Giles JT, *et al*. Arthritis Res Ther, 2012 Feb 24. PMID 22364592, [Free PMC Article](/pmc/articles/PMC3392839/)\n\n[See all (30) citations in PubMed](/pubmed?LinkName=gene_pubmed&from_uid=353238 \"See all 30 citations in Pubmed\")\n\n### [GeneRIFs: Gene References Into Functions](#)\n\n[What's a GeneRIF?](/gene/about-generif)\n\n1.  [Crystal structure of human peptidylarginine deiminase type VI (PAD6) provides insights into its inactivity.](/pubmed/38656308)\n    \n    Title: Crystal structure of human peptidylarginine deiminase type VI (PAD6) provides insights into its inactivity.\n    \n2.  [Case report: human early embryonic arrest in a consanguineous Chinese family caused by a novel missense variant of PADI6.](/pubmed/37220902)\n    \n    Title: Case report: human early embryonic arrest in a consanguineous Chinese family caused by a novel missense variant of PADI6.\n    \n3.  [Novel biallelic mutations in PADI6 in patients with early embryonic arrest.](/pubmed/34987164)\n    \n    Title: Novel biallelic mutations in PADI6 in patients with early embryonic arrest.\n    \n4.  [Genetic Variation in PADI6-PADI4 on 1p36.13 Is Associated with Common Forms of Human Generalized Epilepsy.](/pubmed/34573423)\n    \n    Title: Genetic Variation in PADI6-PADI4 on 1p36.13 Is Associated with Common Forms of Human Generalized Epilepsy.\n    \n5.  [Novel pathogenic variants in NLRP7, NLRP5, and PADI6 in patients with recurrent hydatidiform moles and reproductive failure.](/pubmed/33583041)\n    \n    Title: Novel pathogenic variants in NLRP7, NLRP5, and PADI6 in patients with recurrent hydatidiform moles and reproductive failure.\n    \n6.  [Biallelic PADI6 variants cause multilocus imprinting disturbances and miscarr