rimarily by extrinsic factors, including infections, toxins, nutritional deficiencies, iatrogenic causes, and environmental exposures.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:7770008 ! disease by etiologic mechanism\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770011\nname: disease by molecular mechanism\ndef: \"A grouping class for human diseases classified by their underlying molecular or pathophysiological mechanism, such as protein aggregation, ion channel dysfunction, or signal transduction disruption.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2360-2664]\ncomment: This term is intended solely for classification purposes and should not be used for direct data annotation.\nis_a: MONDO:0700096 ! human disease\n\n","exit":0,"description":"Inspect recent new term metadata examples","truncated":false},"title":"Inspect recent new term metadata examples","time":{"start":1778977527535,"end":1778977527540}},"id":"prt_e3352d6a6001NCRLEPSEPv3O6a","sessionID":"ses_1ccaf3743ffeQMnyfWaPxDVgzw","messageID":"msg_e33528afb001yCPglQTlDb0obi"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977528029,"sessionID":"ses_1ccaf3743ffeQMnyfWaPxDVgzw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_NW3dgfv3aTQzgp80SlwxhtfX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'term_tracker_item|IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo","description":"Check issue tracking metadata patterns"},"output":"...output truncated...\n\nFull output saved to: /github/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_e3352d6d7001GDLWHBR1Kg59FI\n\nxref: GARD:0028185 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0011057 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! cerebrovascular disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0018634 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! hereditary amyloidosis\nis_a: MONDO:0024237 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! inherited neurodegenerative disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/620 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! APP\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9721\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060191\nname: ciliopathy-IFT74\ndef: \"Any ciliopathy caused by variants in the IFT74 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066, PMID:27486776, PMID:33531668, PMID:33748949, PMID:34539760, PMID:37315079, PMID:37555648]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028186\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"ciliopathy-IFT74\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028186 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005308 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066\"} ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005308 ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/21424 ! IFT74\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/21424 {source=\"PMID:37555648\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066\"} ! IFT74\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9732\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060192\nname: CASK-related intellectual disability\ndef: \"A syndromic disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the CASK gene. It is associated with a wide phenotypic spectrum ranging from mild-to-severe intellectual disability with or without nystagmus to moderate-to-profound intellectual disability and progressive microcephaly with pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, often associated with seizures.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:24278995]\nsynonym: \"CASK-related disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:24278995]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0020119 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! X-linked syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: MONDO:0000508 ! syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1497 ! CASK\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9747\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060193\nname: X-linked intellectual disability with or without nystagmus\ndef: \"An X-linked intelelctual disability in which the cause of the disease is hypomorphic CASK pathogenic variants. Affected individuals present with intellectual disability with or without congenital nystagmus. Additional features often include epilepsy, speech impairment, motor delay, and variable brain malformations. Phenotypic severity ranges from mild cognitive impairment to severe developmental disability.\" [PMID:24278995]\nsynonym: \"XLID\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:24278995]\nxref: MEDGEN:476987 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C3275356 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:476987\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0020119 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! X-linked syndromic intellectual disability\nis_a: MONDO:1060192 {source=\"PMID:24278995\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! CASK-related intellectual disability\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1497 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! CASK\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9747\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060194\nname: FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\ndef: \"An autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome that results from defective lymphocyte homoestasis, and is caused by variants in the FAS gene. It is characterized by non-malignant lymphoproliferation, autoimmune disease, and lifelong increased risk for both Hodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphoma.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028187\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028187 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0017979 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0017979 ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 ! FAS\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! FAS\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0004952 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! Hodgkins lymphoma\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0018908 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! non-Hodgkin lymphoma\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9749\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060195\nname: SH2B3-related immune system disorder\ndef: \"A predisposition caused by a mutation in SH2B3 gene that presents with myeloproliferation and/or multi-organ autoimmunity.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related immune system disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related myeloproliferation and autoimmunity\" RELATED [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: MONDO:0020573 ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 ! SH2B3\nintersection_of: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 ! immune system disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! SH2B3\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! immune system disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9576\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060197\nname: congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\ndef: \"A heart disease that is present at birth that occurs with variable extracardiac laterality defects. Features of visceral heterotaxy are not always present but can include abnormal location of the organs within the thoracic, abdominal, or peritoneal cavities. Anatomic and functional problems can include intestinal malrotation leading to volvulus, biliary atresia, and various defects of the central nervous system, urinary tract, and skeleton.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/, PMID:19064609, PMID:30293987, PMID:34666056]\nsynonym: \"congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! congenital heart disease\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9463\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060198\nname: ischemic stroke\ndef: \"A stroke disorder caused by obstruction of blood flow to the brain, due to thrombotic (local blood clot formation) or embolic (due to a blood clot or other material traveling from another site) event.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/stroke/types-of-stroke, https://www.stroke.org.uk/stroke/types, PMID:29763173]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051062\"}\nsynonym: \"ischaemic stroke\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nxref: DOID:0051062 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:215292 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0948008 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:215292\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005098 {source=\"PMID:29763173\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! stroke disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9754\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060199\nname: hemorrhagic stroke\ndef: \"A stroke disorder caused by bleeding into the brain parenchyma or surrounding spaces. Hemorrhagic stroke includes intracerebral hemorrhage (bleeding within the brain tissue) and subarachnoid hemorrhage (bleeding in the space between the brain and the surrounding membrane).\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/stroke/types-of-stroke, https://www.stroke.org.uk/stroke/types, PMID:29763173]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051063\"}\nsynonym: \"haemorrhagic stroke\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nxref: DOID:0051063 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1714259 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5234922 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MEDGEN:1714259\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005098 {source=\"PMID:29763173\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! stroke disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9754\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060200\nname: primary hyperthyroidism\ndef: \"A form of hyperthyroidism caused by overproduction of thyroid hormones (T3 and T4) due to pathology within the thyroid gland itself. Primary hyperthyroidism is characterized by low TSH levels and elevated T3/T4 levels.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nxref: MEDGEN:811409 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C3714618 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:811409\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0004425 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! hyperthyroidism\nintersection_of: MONDO:0004425 ! hyperthyroidism\nintersection_of: disease_has_basis_in_dysfunction_of UBERON:0002046 ! thyroid gland\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060201\nname: secondary hyperthyroidism\ndef: \"A form of hyperthyroidism caused by overproduction of thyroid hormones (T3 and T4) due to pathology outside of the thyroid gland, namely in the hypothalamus or pituitary gland. Secondary hyperthyroidism is characterized by elevated TSH levels and elevated T3/T4 levels.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nxref: MEDGEN:923144 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1095928 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:923144\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0004425 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! hyperthyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060202\nname: toxic thyroid adenoma\ndef: \"A condition in which a single benign adenoma on the thyroid gland  autonomously secretes excessive thyroid hormone, leading to primary hyperthyroidism.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nsubset: inferred_rare\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"toxic adenoma\" EXACT [PMID:30725738]\nxref: MEDGEN:549890 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0302840 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:549890\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005032 {source=\"PMID:32965923\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! follicular thyroid adenoma\nis_a: MONDO:1060200 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! primary hyperthyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060203\nname: hypothalamic hyperthyroidism\ndef: \"A form of secondary hyperthyroidism caused by pathology in the hypothalamus leading to excessive stimulation of the pituitary gland and subsequent overproduction of TSH, resulting in elevated thyroid hormone levels.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:30725738]\nis_a: MONDO:1060201 {source=\"PMID:30725738\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! secondary hyperthyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9759\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060204\nname: menstrual disorder\ndef: \"A disorder of the female reproductive system characterized by abnormalities in the menstrual cycle, including disturbances in timing, flow, or associated pain.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290, PMID:32809669]\nis_a: MONDO:0002263 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! female reproductive system disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060205\nname: dysmenorrhea\ndef: \"A menstrual disorder characterized by pain during the menstrual cycle.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/dysmenorrhea-painful-periods, PMID:32809669]\nxref: MEDGEN:4429 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0013390 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:4429\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060204 {source=\"PMID:32809669\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! menstrual disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060206\nname: primary dysmenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of dysmenorrhea characterized by recurrent menstrual pain without any identifiable underlying pelvic pathology, representing a diagnosis of exclusion. Symptoms typically emerge within two years of menarche.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:32809669]\nxref: MEDGEN:508446 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0149875 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:508446\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060205 {source=\"PMID:32809669\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! dysmenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060207\nname: secondary dysmenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of dysmenorrhea associated with suspected or clinically identifiable pelvic pathology, such as endometriosis, uterine fibroids, or adenomyosis.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:32809669]\nxref: MEDGEN:534931 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0232944 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MEDGEN:534931\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060205 {source=\"PMID:32809669\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! dysmenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060208\nname: primary amenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of amenorrhea defined by the absence of menstruation by the age of 15 years, or by 3 years after the onset of breast development (thelarche).\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290]\nxref: MEDGEN:115918 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0232939 {source=\"MEDGEN:115918\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001836 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! amenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060209\nname: secondary amenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of amenorrhea characterized by the absence of menses for 3 or more months in a woman with previously regular menstrual cycles, or 6 or more months in any woman who has had at least one previous spontaneous menstruation.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290]\nxref: MEDGEN:115919 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0232940 {source=\"MEDGEN:115919\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001836 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! amenorrhea\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060210\nname: functional hypothalamic amenorrhea\ndef: \"A form of secondary amenorrhea caused by suppression of the hypothalamic-pituitary-ovarian axis without identifiable organic pathology, typically associated with energy deficiency, excessive exercise, psychological stress, or low body weight.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:29489290]\nis_a: MONDO:1060209 {source=\"PMID:29489290\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! secondary amenorrhea\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9760\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060211\nname: NR5A1-related sex development disorder\ndef: \"A reproductive system disorder caused by a variation in the NR5A1 gene, and characterized by varying phenotypes, including partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, ambiguous genitalia, and spermatogenic failure in the male, and premature ovarian failure and ovarian dysgenesis in the female.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:28033660, PMID:31513305]\ncomment: 46XY individuals can present with azoospermia, hypospadias, micropenis, cryptorchidism, ambiguous or female-appearing genitalia, partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, Sertoli dysfunction, and progressive testicular failure. Leydig function is often partially preserved, and infertility is common. 46XX individuals can present with primary ovarian insufficiency/ premature ovarian failure, ovarian dysgenesis, and subfertility. Rarely, testicular or ovotesticular disorder of sex development may occur. Individuals typically have normal adrenal function but in rare cases, adrenal insufficiency may be observed in the context of severe-early onset variants.\nsynonym: \"NR5A1-related sex development disorder\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005039 {source=\"PMID:28033660\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005039 ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 ! NR5A1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 {source=\"PMID:28033660\"} ! NR5A1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9863\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060212\nname: CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A syndromic disease caused by a variation in the CRYAB gene, and characterized by a spectrum of phenotypes including cardiomyopathy, cataract, and/or myopathy.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:21920752, PMID:38212463]\nsynonym: \"alpha-B crystallinopathy\" RELATED [PMID:21920752]\nsynonym: \"CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2389 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! CRYAB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9774\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060213\nname: reticular pseudodrusen\ndef: \"A retinal drusen characterized by subretinal deposits located internal to the retinal pigment epithelium, composed of material aggregations in the subretinal space between photoreceptors and the retinal pigment epithelium. These deposits have a bluish-white appearance by biomicroscopy and appear as hyperreflective lesions above the retinal pigment epithelium on optical coherence tomography.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199, PMID:38386332, PMID:41361163]\ncomment: Reticular pseudodrusen are a strong independent risk factor for late age-related macular degeneration and are particularly associated with geographic atrophy and type 3 neovascularization.\nsynonym: \"RPD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199]\nsynonym: \"SDD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199]\nsynonym: \"subretinal drusenoid deposit\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489, PMID:29859199, PMID:38386332]\nxref: SCTID:762533006 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0006949 {source=\"PMID:29859199\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\"} ! retinal drusen\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9849\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060214\nname: SYCE1-related gametogenic failure\ndef: \"An infertility disorder caused by variation in the SYCE1 gene. Affected males may present with non-obstructive azoospermia due to maturation arrest or meiotic failure, while affected females may present with primary ovarian insufficiency.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:32402064, PMID:35718780]\nsynonym: \"SYCE1-related gametogenic failure\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005047 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! infertility disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005047 ! infertility disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28852 ! SYCE1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28852 {source=\"PMID:32402064\", source=\"PMID:35718780\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! SYCE1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9864\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770001\nname: equine juvenile spinocerebellar ataxia, FDXR-related, horse\ndef: \"Any spinocerebellar ataxia that occurs in horses due to a variation in the FDXR gene. EJSCA is a degenerative axonopathy characterized by acute onset of ataxia within the first month of life, affecting the pelvic limbs more severely than the thoracic limb and rapidly progressing to inability to stand.\" [doi:10.1016/j.jevs.2025.105561, PMID:38669583]\nsynonym: \"EJSCA\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:38669583]\nis_a: MONDO:1012960 {source=\"PMID:38669583\"} ! hereditary cerebellar ataxia, non-human animal\nintersection_of: MONDO:1012960 ! hereditary cerebellar ataxia, non-human animal\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100060312 ! FDXR\nintersection_of: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9796 ! Equus caballus\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100060312 {source=\"PMID:38669583\"} ! FDXR\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9796 {source=\"PMID:38669583\"} ! Equus caballus\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9143\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770002\nname: avoidant/restrictive food intake disorder\ndef: \"An eating disorder characterized by avoidance or restriction of food intake due to one or more of the following: lack of interest in eating or food, sensitivity to sensory characteristics of food (such as taste, texture, smell, or appearance), or concern about aversive consequences of eating (such as choking or vomiting), resulting in persistent failure to meet appropriate nutritional and/or energy needs as manifested by significant weight loss, nutritional deficiency, dependence on enteral feeding or nutritional supplements, or marked interference with psychosocial functioning, and where the eating disturbance is not better explained by lack of available food, cultural or religious practices, another mental disorder, or a concurrent medical condition.\" [PMID:38849953]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051057\"}\nsynonym: \"ARFID\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [DOID:0051057, PMID:38849953]\nsynonym: \"selective eating disorder\" EXACT [PMID:38849953]\nxref: DOID:0051057 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:F50.82 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: ICD9:307.59 {source=\"MONDO:relatedTo\"}\nxref: MESH:D000080146 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005451 {source=\"PMID:38849953\"} ! eating disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3311-7320\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9408\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000000\nname: infectious discitis\ndef: \"An infection of the intervertebral disk space.\" [PMID:27070599]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028188\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: EFO:1000900 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:EFO\"}\nxref: GARD:0028188 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005550 {source=\"PMID:27070599\"} ! infectious disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005550 ! infectious disease\nintersection_of: disease_has_inflammation_site UBERON:0001066 ! intervertebral disk\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/501\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000001\nname: staphylococcus discitis\ndef: \"Discitis caused by infection with Staphylococcus.\" [PMID:27070599]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028189\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028189 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:8000000 {source=\"PMID:27070599\"} ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: MONDO:8000000 ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: disease_has_infectious_agent NCBITaxon:1280 ! Staphylococcus aureus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/501\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000002\nname: escherichia coli discitis\ndef: \"Discitis caused by infection with Escherichia coli.\" [PMID:27070599]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028190\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028190 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:8000000 {source=\"PMID:27070599\"} ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: MONDO:8000000 ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: disease_has_infectious_agent NCBITaxon:562 ! Escherichia coli\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/501\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000003\nname: streptococcus pneumoniae discitis\ndef: \"Discitis caused by infection with Streptococcus pneumoniae.\" [PMID:27070599]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028191\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028191 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:8000000 {source=\"PMID:27070599\"} ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: MONDO:8000000 ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: disease_has_infectious_agent NCBITaxon:1313 ! Streptococcus pneumoniae\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/501\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000004\nname: salmonella discitis\ndef: \"Discitis caused by infection with Salmonella.\" [PMID:27070599]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027037\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0027037 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:8000000 {source=\"PMID:27070599\"} ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: MONDO:8000000 ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: disease_has_infectious_agent NCBITaxon:590 ! Salmonella\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/501\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000005\nname: fungal discitis\ndef: \"Discitis caused by infection with fungi.\" [PMID:27070599]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028192\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028192 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1788782 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5547329 {source=\"MEDGEN:1788782\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:8000000 {source=\"PMID:27070599\"} ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: MONDO:8000000 ! infectious discitis\nintersection_of: disease_has_infectious_agent NCBITaxon:4751 ! Fungi\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/501\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000006\nname: WHIM syndrome 1\ndef: \"A congenital autosomal dominant immune deficiency characterized by abnormal retention of mature neutrophils in the bone marrow (myelokathexis) and occasional hypogammaglobulinemia, associated with an increased risk for bacterial infections and a susceptibility to human papillomavirus (HPV) induced lesions (cutaneous warts, genital dysplasia and invasive mucosal carcinoma).\" [Orphanet:51636]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0060591\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:0060591\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0009297\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"NORD:1849\", source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:193670\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:51636\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:51636\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:51636\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"myelokathexis, isolated\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"Warts, hypogammaglobulinemia, infections, and myelokathexis\" EXACT [DOID:0060591]\nsynonym: \"Warts, hypogammaglobulinemia, infections, and myelokathexis syndrome\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"Warts-hypogammaglobulinemia-infections-myelokathexis syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:0060591, Orphanet:51636]\nsynonym: \"Warts